<!--
    Toolbar icons, drawn rather than imported.

    Every icon is path data on the same 24x24 grid with a 3px margin, stroked
    at one weight and never filled, so the set reads as one family and takes
    its colour from the button's foreground - which is what makes it survive
    the light-background switch without a second set of assets. Vector also
    means no bitmap to pick a DPI for; this app is drawing software and a
    fuzzy toolbar at 150% would be embarrassing.

    Node squares (the small boxes on Line, Polyline and Arc) mirror the grips
    the entities will grow in E3, and are what distinguishes an icon for
    "draw a line" from a diagonal stroke.
-->
